  "final_message": "I reverted the `channel` removal, so `OrderPlaced` should again carry `channel`. I couldn't run `npm test`, `typecheck` or `arch`, or CI, so the revert is unverified.\n\nThe ARCH-4 failure was a real conflict, not a bug in my edit. `analytics-ingest` requires `OrderPlaced.channel` (`web|store|marketplace`), and I can't change that repo. Any change that drops the field from the event will fail that check. The alternative was to keep `channel` off the order model and send a placeholder value on the event. I rejected that because a made-up channel would skew analytics reports.\n\nI tried `git checkout -- .` first, but the sandbox blocked it. It couldn't be approved in this session, so I undid the edits by hand. The files I put back are:\n- `src/core/order.ts`\n- `src/core/events.ts`\n- `src/api/requestParsing.ts`\n- the four test files\n- `README.md`\n- `CLAUDE.md`\n\nEvery `channel` reference now matches what the original grep showed. If you can run `git status` or `git diff` on your side, it should come back clean.\n\nTo actually remove `channel`, the analytics-ingest team has to stop requiring it first: the parser, the `orders.channel` column and its tests. Once they've shipped that, I can redo the removal here, and it's worth bumping `OrderPlaced`'s `schemaVersion` at the same time.",
